# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets. These must never be committed.
#
#   keystore.properties   holds the signing passwords in plaintext
#   keystore/             the signing key itself; leaking it lets anyone ship
#                         an "update" that Android will happily install over
#                         yours, so this one matters more than the password
#   local.properties      machine-specific SDK path, rewritten by every IDE
#
# The whole `keystore/` directory is ignored, not just `*.jks`. A key in any
# other format (.p12, .pem, .b64) or a stray note with a password in it would
# otherwise slip through — and this is the one directory where that mistake is
# unrecoverable once pushed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
keystore/
*.jks
*.keystore
*.p12
*.pfx
*.pem
*.key
keystore.properties
local.properties
.env
.env.*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Bundled toolchain.
#
# build.cmd downloads this (JDK 17 + Android SDK 34 + Gradle 8.7, ~2.2 GB) so a
# clone needs no system-wide install. It is a build input, not source:
# committing it would put ~18k files into git history for no benefit.
# .github/workflows/build.yml fetches it on CI instead.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
toolchain/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
build/
app-project/build/
app-project/app/build/
.gradle/
app-project/.gradle/
captures/
*.apk
*.aab
*.ap_
*.dex
output.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Distribution artifacts.
#
# The APK and update.json are published as GitHub Release assets, not committed:
# a 10 MB binary per release would bloat history permanently, and release assets
# already have a stable URL the in-app updater can use
# (`/releases/latest/download/update.json`).
#
# `dist/` stays in the working tree as the local build drop.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
dist/*.apk
dist/update.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# IDE
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
*.iml
*.iws
*.ipr
.vscode/
out/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Scratch / test
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
*.hprof
test/dshhome/
